{"id": "2026-09-12-news-houthis-seize-bab-al-mandab-strait", "date": "2026-09-12", "stream": "news", "headline": "Houthis seize Bab al-Mandab strait", "summary": "Iran-allied Houthis captured Perim island and Mocha port, taking control of the Bab al-Mandab strait and closing the Red Sea to Saudi tankers.", "url": "https://www.lemonde.fr/international/article/2026/09/12/l-arabie-saoudite-isolee-face-a-l-iran-et-aux-rebelles-houthistes-du-yemen-cherche-le-soutien-des-etats-unis_6770908_3210.html", "source_domain": "lemonde.fr", "tier": "T2", "tags": [], "topics": ["geopolitics", "security"], "importance": 3, "display_body": "Iran-allied Houthi forces seized control of the Bab al-Mandab strait — the chokepoint at the southern mouth of the Red Sea — closing the route to Saudi tankers, after capturing the port of Mocha on Thursday 10 September and the strategic island of Perim (Mayoun) on Friday 11 September. Perim splits the strait into two narrow shipping channels at its tightest point and carries its own airstrip, so holding it lets the Houthis command the waterway with coastal artillery rather than the missiles and drones they had relied on. In a statement the group said \"maritime navigation is safe for all companies except for Saudi vessels,\" vowing to strike Saudi targets until \"the aggression stops and the blockade against our dear people is lifted.\" Le Monde called it Saudi Arabia's worst military setback in a decade: with Iran having blockaded the Strait of Hormuz (the Gulf's oil chokepoint) off the kingdom's eastern coast for six months, and the Houthis having bombed the pipeline that carries Saudi crude to the Red Sea on Friday, Riyadh risks losing every maritime outlet for its oil and is now seeking direct US support. Bab al-Mandab normally carries roughly a tenth of world seaborne trade and several million barrels of oil a day.", "why": "two of the three exits for Gulf energy are now contested at once, a step-change in the Iran–Saudi confrontation that threatens global shipping and oil prices well beyond the region.", "thread_id": "2026-09-12-news-houthis-seize-bab-al-mandab-strait", "first_seen_date": "2026-09-12", "event_date": "2026-09-11", "embedding_model": "bge-m3", "emb": "", "entities": ["Houthis", "Bab al-Mandab", "Saudi Arabia", "Iran", "Yemen"]}
{"id": "2026-09-12-news-brics-summit-opens-in-new-delhi", "date": "2026-09-12", "stream": "news", "headline": "BRICS summit opens in New Delhi", "summary": "BRICS summit formally opened in New Delhi with Xi making his first India visit in seven years to join Putin and Iran's Pezeshkian.", "url": "https://www.aljazeera.com/news/2026/9/12/brics-summit-opens-in-new-delhi-amid-wars-global-tensions-tariffs", "source_domain": "aljazeera.com", "tier": "T2", "tags": [], "topics": ["geopolitics"], "importance": 2, "display_body": "The annual BRICS summit — the bloc of major non-Western economies, now marking its 20th year — formally opened in New Delhi on Saturday 12 September, with China's Xi Jinping arriving in India for the first time in seven years to join Russia's Vladimir Putin and Iran's Masoud Pezeshkian. Host Narendra Modi held talks on Friday with Putin (agreeing to deepen ties) and with Pezeshkian (raising freedom of navigation and the safety of ship crews). Also attending are Egypt's Abdel Fattah el-Sisi, Ethiopia's Abiy Ahmed and Indonesia's Prabowo Subianto, plus the WHO and WTO chiefs and UN Secretary-General António Guterres; Brazil's Lula sent his foreign minister. The agenda is dominated by the wars in the Middle East and Ukraine disrupting energy and shipping, US tariffs — President Trump has branded the bloc \"anti-American\" and threatened punitive levies on members — and expanding non-Western cross-border payment channels.", "why": "the Xi–Modi thaw and the choreography of Putin and Pezeshkian in New Delhi is a visible bid by the \"Global South\" to coordinate against Washington's tariff pressure, though the bloc's own divisions (a May foreign-ministers' meeting ended with no joint statement on Iran) limit how far it can go.", "thread_id": "2026-09-11-news-putin-joins-brics-summit-in-new-delhi", "first_seen_date": "2026-09-11", "event_date": "2026-09-11", "embedding_model": "bge-m3", "emb": "", "entities": ["BRICS", "India", "China", "Russia", "Iran"]}
{"id": "2026-09-12-news-france-train-derailment-probed-as-sabotage", "date": "2026-09-12", "stream": "news", "headline": "France train derailment probed as sabotage", "summary": "A Rouen-Caen TER derailed near Cleon injuring 44; police treat deliberate sabotage as the main line of inquiry after finding a rail fragment on the track.", "url": "https://www.lemonde.fr/economie/article/2026/09/11/deraillement-du-ter-rouen-caen-un-bilan-provisoire-d-environ-20-blesses-selon-le-ministre-des-transports_6770640_3234.html", "source_domain": "lemonde.fr", "tier": "T2", "tags": [], "topics": ["world", "security"], "importance": 2, "display_body": "A regional TER (French inter-city train) running from Rouen to Caen derailed near Cléon in Normandy at about 19:45 on Friday 11 September, injuring 44 of the 186 people aboard. An 18-year-old woman was evacuated by helicopter in critical condition and the other 43 were treated for lesser injuries; 130 firefighters, five medical teams and 80 vehicles responded. Investigators are now treating deliberate sabotage as the main line of inquiry after a severed rail fragment was found on the track, according to police sources; the Rouen prosecutor said on Friday night that the cause was not yet established, that the driver's alcohol and drug tests were negative, and that \"the investigation will be long.\"", "why": "if sabotage is confirmed it would be a deliberate attack on France's passenger rail network; for now the malicious-act hypothesis is the lead line, not a finding.", "thread_id": "2026-09-12-news-france-train-derailment-probed-as-sabotage", "first_seen_date": "2026-09-12", "event_date": "2026-09-11", "embedding_model": "bge-m3", "emb": "", "entities": ["France", "SNCF", "Normandy"]}
{"id": "2026-09-12-news-imamoglu-given-new-two-year-sentence", "date": "2026-09-12", "stream": "news", "headline": "Imamoglu given new two-year sentence", "summary": "A Turkish court sentenced jailed Istanbul mayor Ekrem Imamoglu to more than two years in an insult case, with a possible political ban if upheld.", "url": "https://www.turkishminute.com/2026/09/11/jailed-istanbul-mayor-imamoglu-sentenced-to-2-years-in-insult-case/", "source_domain": "turkishminute.com", "tier": "T2", "tags": ["new source"], "topics": ["politics"], "importance": 2, "display_body": "A Turkish court on Friday 11 September sentenced the jailed mayor of Istanbul, Ekrem İmamoğlu, to more than two years in prison in an \"insult\" case, a conviction that could carry a ban from politics if upheld on appeal. İmamoğlu — seen as President Erdoğan's strongest rival and already jailed since earlier this year in a separate corruption case widely condemned as politically driven — was convicted over remarks about the former mayor of Istanbul's Tuzla district. The prison term and the political-rights restrictions under Article 53 of the penal code are not immediately enforceable and take effect only if the conviction becomes final.", "why": "it is the latest in a cascade of prosecutions against Turkey's leading opposition figure, and a political ban would remove him from any future presidential race.", "thread_id": "2026-09-12-news-imamoglu-given-new-two-year-sentence", "first_seen_date": "2026-09-12", "event_date": "2026-09-11", "embedding_model": "bge-m3", "emb": "", "entities": ["Turkey", "Ekrem Imamoglu", "Recep Tayyip Erdogan", "Istanbul"]}
{"id": "2026-09-12-news-sweden-votes-in-knife-edge-election", "date": "2026-09-12", "stream": "news", "headline": "Sweden votes in knife-edge election", "summary": "Sweden holds Riksdag elections on 13 September 2026 with the Red-Green opposition narrowly ahead of the Tido government bloc.", "url": "https://www.riksdagen.se/en/news/the-2026-elections/", "source_domain": "riksdagen.se", "tier": "T1", "tags": ["new source"], "topics": ["politics"], "importance": 2, "display_body": "Sweden votes on Sunday 13 September 2026 in a knife-edge general election, choosing all 349 members of the Riksdag (the national parliament) alongside regional and municipal councils. Recent polling puts the left-leaning Red-Green opposition narrowly ahead of the governing centre-right \"Tidö\" bloc — Prime Minister Ulf Kristersson's Moderates, Christian Democrats and Liberals, who rely on the far-right Sweden Democrats for their majority. One early-September poll gave the opposition an ~8-point lead, but a hung result remains plausible.", "why": "the vote is a test of whether Europe's recent rightward drift stalls or extends, and of the Sweden Democrats' grip on a Nordic government.", "thread_id": "2026-09-12-news-sweden-votes-in-knife-edge-election", "first_seen_date": "2026-09-12", "event_date": "2026-09-13", "embedding_model": "bge-m3", "emb": "", "entities": ["Sweden", "Riksdag", "Sweden Democrats", "Ulf Kristersson"]}
{"id": "2026-09-12-news-school-fire-kills-26-children-in-bukavu", "date": "2026-09-12", "stream": "news", "headline": "School fire kills 26 children in Bukavu", "summary": "A fire and stampede at a school in M23-held Bukavu, eastern DRC, killed at least 26 children on Thursday.", "url": "https://www.lemonde.fr/afrique/article/2026/09/12/rdc-la-mort-d-au-moins-26-ecoliers-apres-un-incendie-a-bukavu-suscite-une-vague-d-emotion-nationale_6770707_3212.html", "source_domain": "lemonde.fr", "tier": "T2", "tags": ["single-source"], "topics": ["world"], "importance": 1, "display_body": "A fire and stampede at a school in Bukavu, in the eastern Democratic Republic of Congo, killed at least 26 children on Thursday 10 September, according to education-ministry inspectors and local authorities. The blaze, of unknown origin, broke out around 9am while pupils were in class; the ensuing panic led to trampling and the asphyxiation of children trapped inside. The M23 armed group (backed by Rwanda), which has controlled Bukavu since February 2025, reported 26 dead — \"20 girls and six boys\" — and declared three days of mourning; both it and the Kinshasa government called for investigations.", "why": "", "thread_id": "2026-09-12-news-school-fire-kills-26-children-in-bukavu", "first_seen_date": "2026-09-12", "event_date": "2026-09-10", "embedding_model": "bge-m3", "emb": "", "entities": ["Democratic Republic of Congo", "Bukavu", "M23"]}
{"id": "2026-09-12-news-lausanne-students-skip-food-to-save-money", "date": "2026-09-12", "stream": "news", "headline": "Lausanne students skip food to save money", "summary": "A survey of 2,500 UNIL students found over a third skipped food or hygiene products and a quarter skipped medical care for cost reasons.", "url": "https://www.srf.ch/news/dialog/umfrage-in-lausanne-studierende-verzichten-auf-essen-und-hygiene", "source_domain": "srf.ch", "tier": "T2", "tags": [], "topics": ["switzerland", "economy"], "importance": 2, "display_body": "More than a third of university students in Lausanne have gone without food or hygiene products for financial reasons, and more than a quarter have skipped medical care, a survey of over 2,500 students by the umbrella body of University of Lausanne (UNIL) student associations found, published this week. Nearly two-thirds cut back on leisure to save money, and the picture of thin margins is stark: almost half say an unexpected 500-franc bill would put them in financial difficulty, and nearly two-thirds could not cover an extra 1,000 francs. Rising rents, food prices and health-insurance premiums were the pressures students cited; the full analysis is due in November 2026.", "why": "it puts a local number on Swiss cost-of-living strain at the sharp end — students rationing basics in one of the country's wealthiest regions.", "thread_id": "2026-09-12-news-lausanne-students-skip-food-to-save-money", "first_seen_date": "2026-09-12", "event_date": "2026-09-12", "embedding_model": "bge-m3", "emb": "", "entities": ["Lausanne", "University of Lausanne"]}
{"id": "2026-09-12-news-vaud-unemployment-rises-to-4-9", "date": "2026-09-12", "stream": "news", "headline": "Vaud unemployment rises to 4.9%", "summary": "Vaud's unemployment rate rose 0.2 point to 4.9% at the end of August 2026, a seasonal rise driven by graduates entering the job market.", "url": "https://www.vd.ch/actualites/communiques-de-presse-de-letat-de-vaud/detail/communique/aout-2026-taux-de-chomage-en-hausse-a-49", "source_domain": "vd.ch", "tier": "T1", "tags": [], "topics": ["switzerland", "economy"], "importance": 1, "display_body": "Unemployment in the canton of Vaud rose 0.2 point to 4.9% at the end of August 2026, ending three months of stability, the cantonal government reported. The rise is seasonal — driven mainly by young people entering the job market after finishing training or studies (under-20s +337, ages 20–29 +344) — rather than a sign of a downturn; the canton counted 21,141 registered unemployed, 879 more than in July. The district of Aigle saw the sharpest increase (5.6%).", "why": "", "thread_id": "2026-09-12-news-vaud-unemployment-rises-to-4-9", "first_seen_date": "2026-09-12", "event_date": "2026-08-31", "embedding_model": "bge-m3", "emb": "", "entities": ["Vaud"]}
